  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 256 PM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nWednesday...Brisk southwest flow aloft prevails. Low and mid \nlevel moisture availability looks scant, thus POPS near zero and\nnegligible. Based on the low and mid level gradients, it looks \nlike it will be windy.\n\nThursday...Similar day to Wednesday with rather strong and dry \nsouthwest flow aloft and decent and deep unidirectional \nsouthwest flow for a windy and dry day.\n\nFriday...The flow backs to south southwest and weakens \nsomewhat, with minor influx of pseudo monsoonal mid level \nmoisture, though confidence in shower and thunderstorms \ndevelopment is negligible thus will keep it dry.\n\nSaturday...Looks like a pseudo moisture tap will emanate up \nfrom the Four Corners with an uptick in PWAT, Precipitable Water\nContent, noted, thus expect isolated to scattered afternoon \nshowers and thunderstorms for our Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges,\nwith the activity spreading northeastward and remaining mostly \nwest of I-25 in the evening.\n\nSunday...Once again, the rather moist southwest flow will tap \npseudo monsoonal moisture and diurnal heating and orographic \neffects will help produce scattered showers and thunderstorms in\nthe afternoon for locations over and near the Snowy and Sierra \nMadre, and northern Laramie Ranges, with the convection \nspreading across the remainder of southeast Wyoming and western \nNebraska in the evening.\n\nMonday...Ridging aloft over the Central Plains states bulges \nwestward across our counties, though with adequate low and mid \nlevel moisture, we still anticipate scattered afternoon and \nevening showers and thunderstorms.",
